      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code and won't start. what am i supposed to do to fix this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The E15 error on your Bosch dishwasher is a classic sign of a water inlet valve issue, but before you panic, you should first check if the water supply valve is fully open, as a partially closed valve is the most common culprit. If the water is flowing, the problem might be a clogged filter or a faulty inlet valve, which requires you to disconnect the power and water supply before inspecting the components. While you are waiting for the water to fill, you might want to check if the drain hose is kinked, as a blocked drain can sometimes cause the machine to think it's full and refuse to start. If you are comfortable with basic plumbing, you can try unscrewing the inlet valve to clear any debris, but if you are not handy, it is best to call a professional technician who has the right tools and experience to diagnose the issue. Remember, if you are not sure about the steps, it is safer to leave the appliance alone and seek expert help to avoid making things worse.\n\n**Quick Fix Steps:**\n1.  **Check the Water Supply:** Ensure the valve under the sink is fully open.\n2.  **Inspect the Filter:** Remove the bottom rack and clean the filter assembly",
